50:                                                         \tag{P3K.31.1}
51: \]
52: where the integral third generator \(\eta\) is normalized so that
53: the stable map \(q\mapsto L_q\), left quaternion multiplication,
54: has degree \(+1\).
55: 
56: The third object is the oriented central return class \(s\in\mathbb Z/28\).
57: The initial delta-retaining family has K23 relative integers
58: \((m,n)\), with
59: \[
60:        V=\operatorname{diag}(v,0,0),\quad
61:        v=-(m+n)=k_{\rm Jin},\quad
62:        \delta=(n-m,0,0)^T,\quad s=A.
63:                                                         \tag{P3K.31.2}
64: \]
65: The formula for \(\delta\) will follow from the literal product-frame
66: comparison below; it is not inferred from an absolute Pontryagin class.
67: 
68: A different global stable frame gives a map from the whole six-sphere
69: to Spin. Its third class is zero because \(H^3(S^6)=0\).
70: K29's exact frame-change pairing therefore shows that (P3K.31.1) is
71: independent of that global choice at the degree being used.
72: No assertion about a higher framing homotopy group is needed.
73: 
74: \par\medskip\noindent\textbf{2. The first-resolution product differs by one normal generator.}\enspace
75: 
